Make declares T without using it in its parameters or results. Declare T on the
generated function and call factory.Make[T](), since Go cannot infer T from the
method call’s arguments.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type Factory struct{}

//plumb:build
func (Factory) Make[T any]() int { return 0 }
